1
00:00:01,300 --> 00:00:06,150
Honey Bunny Kidz presents: Why Doesn't Dotty Duckling Get Wet?

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:11,600
Pitter, patter, pitter, patter.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:14,775
It was a soft, rainy morning.

4
00:00:15,125 --> 00:00:17,600
Pitter, patter, went the rain.

5
00:00:18,350 --> 00:00:22,225
Mama, it's raining! Can we go outside and splash?

6
00:00:22,975 --> 00:00:27,475
Yes, little one! But first, what do we wear in the rain?

7
00:00:27,825 --> 00:00:29,700
Can you guess?

8
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:34,400
A raincoat and rain boots!

9
00:00:34,750 --> 00:00:37,050
You look ready, Honey.

10
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:41,150
My coat is yellow, and my boots are red!

11
00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:47,000
Let's hold hands, stay together, and splash in the little puddles.

12
00:00:49,650 --> 00:00:55,300
Down by the pond, they saw Dotty Duckling, paddling happily in the rain.

13
00:00:56,050 --> 00:00:59,625
Quack, quack! Good morning, Honey!

14
00:00:59,975 --> 00:01:02,600
I love rainy days!

15
00:01:03,350 --> 00:01:06,200
Dotty, you don't have a raincoat!

16
00:01:06,550 --> 00:01:08,625
Aren't you all wet?

17
00:01:09,375 --> 00:01:13,900
Look at my feathers. Are they wet, or dry?

18
00:01:14,250 --> 00:01:16,175
What do you think?

19
00:01:18,175 --> 00:01:22,925
They are dry! The raindrops roll right off me!

20
00:01:23,675 --> 00:01:27,100
Wow! But how? Why don't you get wet, Dotty?

21
00:01:29,750 --> 00:01:38,625
Here is my duck secret. Near my tail, I have a tiny spot that makes a special oil.

22
00:01:39,375 --> 00:01:45,025
I rub the oil on my feathers with my beak, like this.

23
00:01:45,375 --> 00:01:47,725
Rub, rub, rub!

24
00:01:48,475 --> 00:01:51,175
Special oil? That's so clever!

25
00:01:51,925 --> 00:01:54,875
The oil keeps the water out.

26
00:01:55,225 --> 00:01:57,975
So the rain can't soak in.

27
00:01:58,325 --> 00:02:01,325
My feathers are waterproof!

28
00:02:02,075 --> 00:02:05,050
See the raindrops on my back?

29
00:02:05,400 --> 00:02:08,825
They sit like shiny little beads.

30
00:02:09,175 --> 00:02:12,650
Let's count them as they roll off.

31
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:14,400
Ready?

32
00:02:15,600 --> 00:02:17,800
One. Two. Three!

33
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:21,425
Roll, roll, roll! Off they go!

34
00:02:24,075 --> 00:02:25,075
Splash!

35
00:02:25,475 --> 00:02:29,700
Splash! Here came Pip Puppy, hopping through the puddles.

36
00:02:30,450 --> 00:02:33,441
Hello, friends! Oh, my fur is all drippy!

37
00:02:34,191 --> 00:02:37,866
Pip's fur gets wet, but Dotty's feathers stay dry.

38
00:02:38,216 --> 00:02:41,316
Everybody is made in a special way!

39
00:02:42,066 --> 00:02:44,477
Do you know what puppies do when we're wet?

40
00:02:44,827 --> 00:02:46,322
Can you guess?

41
00:02:48,322 --> 00:02:50,443
We shake! Shake, shake, shake!

42
00:02:51,193 --> 00:02:54,474
Shake with me! Wiggle your head, wiggle your arms.

43
00:02:54,824 --> 00:02:56,565
Shake, shake, shake!

44
00:02:58,065 --> 00:03:01,365
Hee hee! Little drops everywhere!

45
00:03:02,115 --> 00:03:05,965
Mama Bunny wrapped Pip in a soft, warm towel.

46
00:03:06,315 --> 00:03:09,890
Next time, Pip will wear his raincoat too.

47
00:03:12,540 --> 00:03:15,615
Now let's jump in the puddles!

48
00:03:15,965 --> 00:03:18,565
Stomp your feet with us!

49
00:03:19,315 --> 00:03:21,940
Splish, splash, puddle jump!

50
00:03:22,290 --> 00:03:24,590
Stomp, stomp, stomp!

51
00:03:25,340 --> 00:03:26,340
Splash!

52
00:03:26,740 --> 00:03:29,151
Splish, splash, puddle jump!

53
00:03:29,501 --> 00:03:31,175
Hop, hop, hop!

54
00:03:31,925 --> 00:03:32,925
Splash!

55
00:03:33,325 --> 00:03:36,800
Splish, splash, one more jump!

56
00:03:37,150 --> 00:03:39,525
Quack, quack, quack!

57
00:03:40,275 --> 00:03:41,275
Splash!

58
00:03:41,675 --> 00:03:44,925
What does a duck say? Can you say it, too?

59
00:03:46,925 --> 00:03:50,325
Quack, quack! What a great quack!

60
00:03:52,975 --> 00:03:55,750
Dotty, how do you swim so fast?

61
00:03:56,500 --> 00:04:02,600
Look at my feet! They are wide and flat, like little paddles.

62
00:04:03,350 --> 00:04:09,775
Ducks have webbed feet. There is soft skin between their toes, so they can push the water.

63
00:04:10,125 --> 00:04:12,100
Paddle, paddle!

64
00:04:12,850 --> 00:04:16,700
Can you make your hands into duck feet?

65
00:04:17,050 --> 00:04:19,625
Paddle, paddle, paddle!

66
00:04:21,625 --> 00:04:24,275
Paddle, paddle! Look, I'm a duck!

67
00:04:24,625 --> 00:04:25,775
Quack!

68
00:04:28,425 --> 00:04:32,150
Then the rain went slow, and slower, and stopped.

69
00:04:32,500 --> 00:04:35,125
The sun came out to say hello.

70
00:04:35,875 --> 00:04:39,200
Look! A rainbow! What colors can you see?

71
00:04:41,200 --> 00:04:45,025
Red, orange, yellow, green, blue, and purple!

72
00:04:45,775 --> 00:04:53,725
Rain is good for the flowers, good for the pond, and good for little ducks like me!

73
00:04:54,475 --> 00:04:58,425
Let's take a big breath of fresh, rainy-day air.

74
00:04:58,775 --> 00:05:01,175
Breathe in, slowly.

75
00:05:02,675 --> 00:05:05,300
And breathe out. Ahhh.

76
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:11,275
Today I learned a duck secret!

77
00:05:11,625 --> 00:05:16,100
Dotty's feathers have special oil, so the rain rolls right off.

78
00:05:16,850 --> 00:05:19,700
And you have a raincoat, Honey!

79
00:05:20,050 --> 00:05:22,525
We both stay cosy.

80
00:05:23,275 --> 00:05:25,485
And I have a big shake! Woof!

81
00:05:26,235 --> 00:05:29,360
Everybody is made in a special way.

82
00:05:29,710 --> 00:05:32,210
Thank you for splashing with us!

83
00:05:32,560 --> 00:05:35,460
See you next time on Honey Bunny Kidz.
